## What to deliver

Build and rig the reliquary up operation by operation until each `parts/<part>.png`
matches the brief, the assembled `scene/` previews show the parts fitting together
correctly, and the rig is complete: a tall masonry plinth and cradle, a glowing solar
core at its heart, an orbital ring encircling it, and guardian fins crowning it.
**Author the three required animations** as F-curves with the `voxel-anim` animation
subcommands: `ring_spin` (a smooth, steady full revolution of the ring), `core_pulse`
(a slow breathing rise-and-settle of the core, eased so the breath carries weight), and
`fins_spin` (a full revolution of the fins the OPPOSITE way from the ring, so they
visibly counter-rotate) — all three self-playing, so the monument cycles on its own
while the plinth stays fixed. The animations are the fixed contract — produce all three,
by those names; the parts and joints that realize them are yours. When you are
satisfied, stop: the recorded per-part logs and `rig.json` are your finished submission.
